--- F-12 INVESTIGATION  (work/s6-outofview-getnext.log) ---------------------  14:41:4x
A walk that times out could be a broken instrument, a throttled agent or a product defect.
Separated with four controlled probes:
  control, permitted GET .1.3.6.1.2.1.1.5.0           -> VALUE "awplus"      (instrument alive)
  GETNEXT inside the view, .1.3.6.1.2.1.1.1.0         -> VALUE .1.3.6.1.2.1.1.2.0
  GETNEXT on the LAST in-view OID .1.3.6.1.2.1.1.9.1.4.8, timeout 5 s, 2 retries
                                                      -> Timeout: No Response
  GETNEXT outside the view, .1.3.6.1.2.1.2.1, timeout 5 s, 3 retries
                                                      -> Timeout: No Response
  control again, permitted GET .1.3.6.1.2.1.1.5.0     -> VALUE "awplus"      (still alive)
  => The agent is not dead, not throttled and not slow: an in-view GetNext is answered in
  milliseconds between two silences. The agent is SILENT, specifically and repeatably, when a
  GetNext's successor OID falls outside the requesting user's MIB view, even with a 5 s
  timeout and 3 retries. A GET of an out-of-view OID is answered correctly with noSuchObject;
  only GetNext is silent. RFC 3416 §4.2.2 requires the varbind to be returned with the value
  endOfMibView. Logged as F-12. Practical consequence: snmpwalk against any view-restricted
  SNMPv3 user cannot terminate cleanly on this build -- it stalls at the view boundary and
  ends in a client timeout.

