   changed.
N2 O-9: AWPTCM-T43870's authored precondition cannot pass as written -- the group reads a
   view the block never defines. This case was run with that one line supplied, and said so
   everywhere. If you would rather have the verbatim-config result recorded as the verdict,
   leg A is in work/s3-legA-verbatim.log and the case would be FAIL on authored step 4. The
   grading here treats it as a case defect, not a platform defect, because the credentials
   demonstrably worked and only the view name was missing.
N3 F-12 is a genuine RFC 3416 deviation with an operator-visible consequence (snmpwalk cannot
   terminate against a view-restricted v3 user). It deserves a developer's eye.
N4 Memory `ckdb-case-lookup-by-title` is wrong and should be corrected at wrap, as triage
   also said: the first lookup is `zephyr_cases` keyed on `AWPTCM-T<id>`. tools/ckcase.py now
   does it in one command.
N5 `tools/tb` did not work on tb277 before this run (the box's `python3` is 3.6; queue
   RISK-7). Fixed generically rather than worked around: `tb277` was added to the wrapper's
   BOX_PY map so it picks `python3.8`, exactly as tb105 already did. Every gate and every
   console step in this case then went through `tools/tb`, per Ask-CK decision D6. RISK-7 can
   be closed.

